# Code Conventions

## Components

- Functional components + hooks ONLY (no class components)
- Props interface: `{ComponentName}Props`
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Colocated tests: `ComponentName.test.tsx`

## TypeScript

- Strict mode — no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for simple types
- Import types: `import type { X } from "..."`

## Files

- kebab-case for files: `element-utils.ts`
- PascalCase for components: `LayerUI.tsx`

## How to Verify

### Code Review Checklist

- [ ] **No class components**: Search for `class.*extends` in the file
- [ ] **Props interface exists**: Component has `{ComponentName}Props` type/interface
- [ ] **Named exports only**: No `export default` statements
- [ ] **No `any` types**: Search for `: any` or `as any`
- [ ] **No `@ts-ignore`**: Verify file doesn't contain `@ts-ignore`
- [ ] **Import types correctly**: Type imports use `import type` syntax
- [ ] **Naming conventions**: Files use kebab-case, components use PascalCase
- [ ] **Test file exists**: Component has corresponding `.test.tsx` file

### Automated Checks

```bash
# Find class components
rg "class\s+\w+\s+extends" packages/ --type ts --type tsx

# Find any types
rg ":\s*any" packages/ --type ts --type tsx

# Find @ts-ignore
rg "@ts-ignore" packages/ --type ts --type tsx

# Find default exports
rg "export\s+default" packages/ --type ts --type tsx

# Find missing import type
rg "import\s+\{\s*\w+.*\}\s+from" packages/ --type ts --type tsx
```